Read fatal errors directly from ProcessNewBlock in submission callers. Test
block-write, undo-write, and post-validation flush failures, including the
absence of BlockChecked signals for fatal validation failures.

Fatal AcceptBlock and ConnectBlock failures no longer emit BlockChecked,
since callers now receive the error from ProcessNewBlock. Clean up the
submitted block source in peer processing when ProcessNewBlock returns a
fatal error.

For block submission over the mining interface, a fatal error is reported
with reason "inconclusive" and the error message in debug, so that reason
keeps its existing set of values.

Co-authored-by: Hodlinator <172445034+hodlinator@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-authored-by: optout <13562139+optout21@users.noreply.github.com>

48aa22c42b remove FatalError() function

b19363fad9 consensus: remove ValidationState error mode

Runtime failures are now returned separately through `util::Expected`, so `ValidationState`
only needs to represent valid and invalid validation outcomes.
Remove `M_ERROR`, `Error()`, and `IsError()`.

ebe01e1c00 kernel: remove INTERNAL_ERROR validation mode

Validation state no longer represents runtime failures, so remove INTERNAL_ERROR from the kernel C API and C++ wrapper.
